    "scope": "One TOML document from local bytes passed to Toml::parse(string). The array API (parseToArray/toArray) cannot tell a local date-time or local date from an offset date-time (all DateTimeImmutable) and returns local times as plain strings, so the harness reads the scalar kinds from the documented AST value nodes and places them exactly where Document::toArray() places their values. Offset date-times are converted to the UTC instant from the returned DateTimeImmutable; local times keep the library's LocalTimeValue string with trailing fractional zeros dropped. Both valid controls match the hand-written typed trees exactly (table keys sorted).",
    "family": "internal/toml (php-internal/toml) Lexer, recursive-descent Parser and AST",
    "family_note": "Own character Lexer (src/Parser/Lexer.php) and Parser (src/Parser/Parser.php) build an AST of Entry/Table/TableArray and typed value nodes; Document::toArray() assembles tables, dotted keys and arrays of tables. No delegation to another TOML parser and no code shared with yosymfony/toml, devium/toml or php-collective/toml.",
